#====================================================================
# DRAFT-swftools-autotools-hmdfs-2168 - Harden legacy Autotools packages on OHOS/HMDFS
#====================================================================

id:                     E491
trigger_tool:           configure|make|conan|ld.lld
phase:                  configure|build|package|testing
error_signature:        Permission denied.*configure|cannot create.*subs1\.awk|multiple definition|install.*(/bin|/share)

severity:               2
category:               hmdfs, autotools, legacy-c, staged-install
match_keywords:         swftools, Autotools, configure, HMDFS, TMPDIR, umask, fno-common, DESTDIR, Makefile.in, Conan, OHOS
title:                  Harden legacy Autotools packages for HMDFS and staged OHOS installs

root_cause:             Legacy generated Autotools files can assume directly executable source scripts, private temporary directories that remain usable by child processes, common-symbol merging, and recursive install rules that honor the selected prefix without an explicit staging root. These assumptions fail independently on OHOS/HMDFS and with modern Clang defaults.
affected_scope:         Legacy Autotools command-line packages built in OHOS/HMDFS workspaces and installed into isolated Conan package directories.
verification_cmd:       Confirm the official swftools-0.9.2 archive declares lib/python test1-test6 and lib/action test but omits their six test_*.py scripts and test.c, recording N_declared=7 and N_runnable=0; then run a clean single-package build on the HarmonyOS PC runner and require configure/build/install, package signing, and the swfc -> SWF -> swfdump test_package path (M=1) to pass 1/1.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           patch-each-autotools-failure-layer-and-run-end-to-end
rec_description:        Invoke a readable configure script through sh when direct execution is unreliable; create a per-build writable TMPDIR with compatible permissions; replace tentative definitions with extern declarations plus one definition; propagate DESTDIR through every recursive Makefile.in install rule; distinguish declared upstream tests from files actually present in the release archive; then validate a real generated artifact with another packaged command.
rec_command:            sh configure <args> && make -j1 && make DESTDIR=<package-root> install
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch|conan-recipe|test-package

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      isolate-and-classify-each-build-stage
fallback_description:   If the package still fails, separate script execution, configure temporary files, compilation/linking, recursive install, signing, and runtime validation so an environment resource failure is not misclassified as a library defect.
fallback_command:       Re-run only after checking device process and memory pressure, preserving the same source and recipe revision.
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          diagnostic-workflow

forbid_1_pattern:       (^|\s)-fcommon(\s|$)
forbid_1_reason:        A global compiler compatibility flag hides invalid declaration/definition relationships in old source code.
forbid_1_consequence:   Duplicate or ambiguous global state remains and can fail again under another compiler or link mode.

forbid_2_pattern:       make install(?!.*DESTDIR)
forbid_2_reason:        A prefix alone does not protect the target root when legacy recursive install rules use absolute bin, share, or man paths.
forbid_2_consequence:   Packaging can write outside the Conan package directory or fail on protected target directories.

forbid_3_pattern:       retry.*(can't fork|Errno 12)
forbid_3_reason:        Process or memory exhaustion must be classified with device resource evidence before changing package code.
forbid_3_consequence:   Repeated heavy runs consume the shared device window and can produce unrelated recipe changes.

principles:             P003, P005, P013
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:

